Fixed. `Cart.total()` in `shop/cart.py:29` was taxing the full subtotal and then subtracting the discount (`subtotal + tax - discount`), instead of taxing the post-discount amount as the docstring intended. That's why the SAVE20 order came out to $90 instead of $88. Changed it to discount first, then tax on the discounted amount — all 5 tests in `shop/test_cart.py` now pass, and I posted the root cause and fix to SHOP-142.
